 "title": "Row-linear separation for bit LeftPigeon is a static kernel question",
 "subject": "The binary left-pigeon principle, PPADS-complete, in polynomial calculus and resolution over parities",
 "conclusion": "For the binary left-pigeon principle, a row-linear polynomial derived in polynomial-calculus degree B, with 2lB - 1 <= n, lies in a fixed kernel of the decoder to Braun's unary pigeonhole system; that kernel contains the inverse-counting identities, summing over holes equals summing over pigeons, and at degree 2 it is a fraction near (l+1)^2 k / v of the row-linear space.",
